## Migration Analysis

Your code has three patterns that break on .NET 8:

| Pattern | Issue on .NET 8 |
|---------|----------------|
| `Thread.Abort()` | Throws `PlatformNotSupportedException` (SYSLIB0006) |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | Obsolete (SYSLIB0046 in .NET 9), unreliable wake mechanism |
| `ManualResetEvent.WaitOne()` + Interrupt | Can't be cooperatively cancelled |

## Migrated Code

```csharp
public class EventProcessor : IDisposable
{
    private readonly Channel<string> _channel = Channel.CreateUnbounded<string>();
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();
    private Task? _processTask;

    public void Start()
    {
        _processTask = Task.Run(() => RunLoopAsync(_cts.Token));
    }

    private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
    {
        await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
        {
            Handle(item);
        }
    }

    public void Enqueue(string item)
    {
        _channel.Writer.TryWrite(item);
    }

    public async Task StopAsync()
    {
        _channel.Writer.Complete();      // signal no more items
        _cts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5)); // timeout fallback

        if (_processTask is not null)
            await _processTask.ConfigureAwait(false);
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _cts.Dispose();
    }

    private void Handle(string item) { /* your logic */ }
}
```

**Required using:**
```csharp
using System.Threading.Channels;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
```

## Key Changes

| Before (.NET Framework) | After (.NET 8) |
|------------------------|----------------|
| `Thread` + `ManualResetEvent` | `Task.Run` + `Channel<T>` |
| `lock` + `Queue<string>` | `Channel<string>` (thread-safe by design) |
| `Thread.Interrupt()` | `Channel.Writer.Complete()` |
| `Thread.Abort()` | `CancellationTokenSource.CancelAfter(5s)` |
| Synchronous `Stop()` | Async `StopAsync()` |

## Pitfalls to Watch

1. **`Handle()` must cooperate** — If `Handle` does long-running work, pass the token into it and check `token.ThrowIfCancellationRequested()` at checkpoints, otherwise the 5s timeout won't interrupt it.

2. **Dispose the CTS** — `CancellationTokenSource` leaks timers if not disposed. Implement `IDisposable`.

3. **Graceful vs forced stop** — `Writer.Complete()` lets in-flight items drain. The `CancelAfter` is the hard deadline. Tune the timeout to your needs.

4. **Exception handling** — `ReadAllAsync` throws `OperationCanceledException` when the token fires. Wrap `RunLoopAsync` in try/catch if you need cleanup:

```csharp
private async Task RunLoopAsync(CancellationToken token)
{
    try
    {
        await foreach (var item in _channel.Reader.ReadAllAsync(token))
            Handle(item);
    }
    catch (OperationCanceledException) { /* timeout hit, exit gracefully */ }
}
```

5. **If you need synchronous `Stop()`** (e.g., called from a non-async context):

```csharp
public void Stop()
{
    _channel.Writer.Complete();
    _cts.CancelAfter(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
    _processTask?.GetAwaiter().GetResult();
}
```

This fully replaces `Thread.Abort`/`Interrupt` with cooperative cancellation — the only model supported on .NET 8.
